From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:57:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Added a scheduled local copy of the CISA KEV catalog and
 EPSS scores

A new vulnintel app keeps CISA's Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog and
FIRST's EPSS scores for the CVE IDs findings reference. Both sources are off
by default. The Vulnerability Intelligence Configuration page enables them,
sets the update frequency and run time, and owns the Django Q schedule that
runs the refresh. It also shows run status and has a Refresh Now button.

Downloads use HTTPS with verified certificates and are checked for size,
shape and age before anything is stored. Each source updates independently.
A CVE ID newly added to a finding is looked up through FIRST's API.
import_kev, import_epss and refresh_vuln_intel cover offline servers and the
command line. The data is read-only in the admin panel and in GraphQL for
the user and manager roles.

